"""
The Linux driver-domain kernel as a package derivation
(docs/spectrum_plan.md §3.4, Sprint 7 task 7.1).

Data-only recipe: it pins the *kconfig intent* of SpectrumOS's reference
driver VM (`../spectrum/vm/sys/net/default.nix`, read firsthand) — the
virtio/erofs enabling set and the console/VT baggage removal — plus the
stripped-vmlinux install target that same file names. Nothing else is
claimed:

  * `sources` is empty for the same recorded reason as the Bootstrap seed
    set (PLAN_avm_pkg §4.8 supplier note): there is no kernel source
    payload in this workspace to hash, and naming an unhashed digest would
    claim an input the store cannot resolve;
  * `builder_symbol` is `linux.build` with an explicit `BUILDER_STATUS`
    env row: no kernel-compiling builder exists here (no kernel sources,
    machine is offline). The evaluation path honest-refuses on an unknown
    builder rather than pretending — this is exactly the Sprint-7 row the
    plan records as *not covered* with its capable-host reproduction
    commands (docs/spectrum_plan.md §6).

Exported through `austral compile … --pkg-totality=true
--emit-derivations=plan.json` and hashed by `avm-pkg drv-hash`, same
release contract as the seed package set (PLAN_avm_pkg §4.8).
"""
import Derivation (
    Derivation
);

module LinuxDriverKernel is
    constant linux_driver_kernel: Derivation;
end module.